      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787092948138,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HLD COMPONENT BEST PRACTICES",
      "originalText": "HLD COMPONENT BEST PRACTICES",
      "fontSize": 34.06,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b0Z"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3BPLeftBody1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1943.7887999739823,
      "y": 2024.3518753558428,
      "width": 1650,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "HnMfl3zUaLJez2eI6LWk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3048,
      "version": 408,
      "versionNonce": 1000543951,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787092948138,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CDN\n• Fingerprinted filenames → Cache-Control: immutable, max-age=31536000\n• API responses: Surrogate-Control: max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=30\n• Origin shield: single PoP → reduces origin hits 10–30×\n• Providers: CloudFront (AWS), Cloudflare (DDoS+WAF), Fastly (real-time config)\n• Skip CDN: user-specific data, write paths, regulated data residency\n\nLOAD BALANCER\n• L7 ALB: host/path routing, SSL termination, WebSocket upgrade\n• L4 NLB: ultra-low latency, no HTTP context — gaming, DB proxy\n• Health: active (/health HTTP) + passive (5xx rate tracking)\n• Connection draining: 30s grace before removing unhealthy instance\n• Avoid sticky sessions: use Redis for sessions → stateless LB\n\nAPI GATEWAY\n• Responsibilities: auth, rate limit, routing, SSL, transform, logging\n• Managed: AWS API GW (pay-per-call) | Self-hosted: Kong, Traefik\n• Anti-pattern: business logic in gateway (gateway = infrastructure only)\n• Rate limit: token bucket in Redis, return 429 + Retry-After header\n• Circuit breaker at gateway → prevents cascade to all downstream services\n\nCACHE (Redis)\n• Key design: namespace:type:id (user:profile:123) → enables pattern delete\n• TTL: shorter = fresh | longer = DB relief; stale-while-revalidate pattern\n• Thundering herd: probabilistic early expiry OR mutex on first miss\n• Hot key: key + rand(0, N) → distribute reads across N virtual shards\n• Redis Cluster: 16384 hash slots, auto failover; cross-slot ops restricted\n• Do NOT cache: financial real-time data, low-read-frequency entities\n\nMESSAGE QUEUE\n• Kafka: ordered per partition, durable log, replay up to N months\n  Partition key = entity_id (preserves ordering per entity)\n  Consumer group = horizontal scale (up to partition count)\n• SQS: visibility timeout > max processing time; DLQ after N retries\n• Idempotency: consumer MUST store processed event_ids before processing\n• Outbox pattern: write event + state in same DB tx → relay publishes\n  Eliminates dual-write inconsistency between state and event store",
      "originalText": "CDN\n• Fingerprinted filenames → Cache-Control: immutable, max-age=31536000\n• API responses: Surrogate-Control: max-age=60, stale-while-revalidate=30\n• Origin shield: single PoP → reduces origin hits 10–30×\n• Providers: CloudFront (AWS), Cloudflare (DDoS+WAF), Fastly (real-time config)\n• Skip CDN: user-specific data, write paths, regulated data residency\n\nLOAD BALANCER\n• L7 ALB: host/path routing, SSL termination, WebSocket upgrade\n• L4 NLB: ultra-low latency, no HTTP context — gaming, DB proxy\n• Health: active (/health HTTP) + passive (5xx rate tracking)\n• Connection draining: 30s grace before removing unhealthy instance\n• Avoid sticky sessions: use Redis for sessions → stateless LB\n\nAPI GATEWAY\n• Responsibilities: auth, rate limit, routing, SSL, transform, logging\n• Managed: AWS API GW (pay-per-call) | Self-hosted: Kong, Traefik\n• Anti-pattern: business logic in gateway (gateway = infrastructure only)\n• Rate limit: token bucket in Redis, return 429 + Retry-After header\n• Circuit breaker at gateway → prevents cascade to all downstream services\n\nCACHE (Redis)\n• Key design: namespace:type:id (user:profile:123) → enables pattern delete\n• TTL: shorter = fresh | longer = DB relief; stale-while-revalidate pattern\n• Thundering herd: probabilistic early expiry OR mutex on first miss\n• Hot key: key + rand(0, N) → distribute reads across N virtual shards\n• Redis Cluster: 16384 hash slots, auto failover; cross-slot ops restricted\n• Do NOT cache: financial real-time data, low-read-frequency entities\n\nMESSAGE QUEUE\n• Kafka: ordered per partition, durable log, replay up to N months\n  Partition key = entity_id (preserves ordering per entity)\n  Consumer group = horizontal scale (up to partition count)\n• SQS: visibility timeout > max processing time; DLQ after N retries\n• Idempotency: consumer MUST store processed event_ids before processing\n• Outbox pattern: write event + state in same DB tx → relay publishes\n  Eliminates dual-write inconsistency between state and event store",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b0a"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3BPRightBody",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3604.0801117677092,
      "y": 2038.382290953029,
      "width": 783.4346561552052,
      "height": 900,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "HnMfl3zUaLJez2eI6LWk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3049,
      "version": 679,
      "versionNonce": 349815201,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787092948138,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "DATABASE\n• Connection pool: PgBouncer (PG), ProxySQL (MySQL)\n  Pool size = (cores × 2) + disk spindle count (empirical rule)\n• Read replicas: route 80% of reads; monitor lag (alert >5s)\n• EXPLAIN ANALYZE: every query >100ms; cover WHERE + ORDER BY cols\n• Partial index: WHERE is_active = true (smaller, faster, targeted)\n• Expand-contract migration: add nullable → backfill → add constraint\n  (zero-downtime; never add NOT NULL to existing table directly)\n• N+1: detect via log_min_duration_statement; fix with JOINs or DataLoader\n\nOBSERVABILITY\n• Metrics (RED per service): Rate, Error rate, Duration P50/P99\n• Metrics (USE per infra): Utilization, Saturation, Errors\n• SLO alerts: burn-rate (fast 5m + slow 6h windows) > threshold alerts\n• Logs: structured JSON; always include trace_id, span_id, service, level\n  Never log raw: passwords, tokens, PII fields\n• Traces: OpenTelemetry → Jaeger/Tempo; W3C TraceContext headers\n  Sample: 100% of errors + 1% of success traces (cost control)\n• Synthetic: probe golden-path every 60s from 3+ regions\n\nSERVICE-TO-SERVICE\n• Sync (gRPC): set deadline on every call (never infinite wait)\n  Retry only idempotent calls; non-idempotent needs idempotency-key\n• Async (Kafka/SQS): producer fires-and-forgets; consumer idempotent\n• Timeout hierarchy: outer client deadline → propagate through each hop\n  Never set inner timeout longer than outer (wasted work)\n• mTLS: zero-trust; Istio/Linkerd service mesh automates cert rotation\n• Service discovery: K8s DNS (in-cluster), Consul (multi-cluster/cloud)\n\nSECURITY BASELINE (every production system)\n• All DBs in private subnets (no public route, SG from svc layer only)\n• All secrets in Secrets Manager / Vault (never plaintext in env vars)\n• TLS 1.3 everywhere; mTLS between internal services\n• WAF in front of CDN (OWASP managed rules, DDoS protection)\n• Audit logs: every data-access event with actor, resource, timestamp\n• Zero-trust: no implicit trust even on internal network — verify every hop",
      "originalText": "DATABASE\n• Connection pool: PgBouncer (PG), ProxySQL (MySQL)\n  Pool size = (cores × 2) + disk spindle count (empirical rule)\n• Read replicas: route 80% of reads; monitor lag (alert >5s)\n• EXPLAIN ANALYZE: every query >100ms; cover WHERE + ORDER BY cols\n• Partial index: WHERE is_active = true (smaller, faster, targeted)\n• Expand-contract migration: add nullable → backfill → add constraint\n  (zero-downtime; never add NOT NULL to existing table directly)\n• N+1: detect via log_min_duration_statement; fix with JOINs or DataLoader\n\nOBSERVABILITY\n• Metrics (RED per service): Rate, Error rate, Duration P50/P99\n• Metrics (USE per infra): Utilization, Saturation, Errors\n• SLO alerts: burn-rate (fast 5m + slow 6h windows) > threshold alerts\n• Logs: structured JSON; always include trace_id, span_id, service, level\n  Never log raw: passwords, tokens, PII fields\n• Traces: OpenTelemetry → Jaeger/Tempo; W3C TraceContext headers\n  Sample: 100% of errors + 1% of success traces (cost control)\n• Synthetic: probe golden-path every 60s from 3+ regions\n\nSERVICE-TO-SERVICE\n• Sync (gRPC): set deadline on every call (never infinite wait)\n  Retry only idempotent calls; non-idempotent needs idempotency-key\n• Async (Kafka/SQS): producer fires-and-forgets; consumer idempotent\n• Timeout hierarchy: outer client deadline → propagate through each hop\n  Never set inner timeout longer than outer (wasted work)\n• mTLS: zero-trust; Istio/Linkerd service mesh automates cert rotation\n• Service discovery: K8s DNS (in-cluster), Consul (multi-cluster/cloud)\n\nSECURITY BASELINE (every production system)\n• All DBs in private subnets (no public route, SG from svc layer only)\n• All secrets in Secrets Manager / Vault (never plaintext in env vars)\n• TLS 1.3 everywhere; mTLS between internal services\n• WAF in front of CDN (OWASP managed rules, DDoS protection)\n• Audit logs: every data-access event with actor, resource, timestamp\n• Zero-trust: no implicit trust even on internal network — verify every hop",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b0b"
    },
    {
      "id": "g3TitleSecC01",
      "type": "text",
