      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787191328894,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Alex Xu — \"System Design Interview: An Insider's Guide\" (Vol. 1 & 2) — the de facto interview-prep book; complements DDIA's depth with interview framing and pacing.\n- roadmap.sh/system-design — free, actively maintained community roadmap and topic breakdown.\n- donnemartin/system-design-primer (GitHub) — large open-source collection of system design notes, diagrams, and flashcards.\n- AWS Architecture Center (aws.amazon.com/architecture) — reference architectures and the AWS Well-Architected Framework whitepapers for real tradeoff examples.\n- Google Cloud Architecture Center (cloud.google.com/architecture) — official reliability/scalability patterns, similar in spirit to AWS's.\n- Netflix Tech Blog (netflixtechblog.com) — production war-stories on chaos engineering, resilience, and real-world failure modes.\n- \"The Log: What every software engineer should know about real-time data's unifying abstraction\" — Jay Kreps, LinkedIn Engineering blog — canonical explainer underlying Kafka-style architectures.\n- High Scalability (highscalability.com) — long-running blog of real company architecture case studies.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Alex Xu — \"System Design Interview: An Insider's Guide\" (Vol. 1 & 2) — the de facto interview-prep book; complements DDIA's depth with interview framing and pacing.\n- roadmap.sh/system-design — free, actively maintained community roadmap and topic breakdown.\n- donnemartin/system-design-primer (GitHub) — large open-source collection of system design notes, diagrams, and flashcards.\n- AWS Architecture Center (aws.amazon.com/architecture) — reference architectures and the AWS Well-Architected Framework whitepapers for real tradeoff examples.\n- Google Cloud Architecture Center (cloud.google.com/architecture) — official reliability/scalability patterns, similar in spirit to AWS's.\n- Netflix Tech Blog (netflixtechblog.com) — production war-stories on chaos engineering, resilience, and real-world failure modes.\n- \"The Log: What every software engineer should know about real-time data's unifying abstraction\" — Jay Kreps, LinkedIn Engineering blog — canonical explainer underlying Kafka-style architectures.\n- High Scalability (highscalability.com) — long-running blog of real company architecture case studies.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "index": "b1S"
